    'UAE GCAA CAR Part XI Issue 04 November 2020 — 18.3 all on aerodrome developments which could have an impact on any supplementary water supply (hydrant) should be assessed; Appendix 3.1.4 availability of supplementary water supplies to be described within the Aerodrome Manual including the policy for any operation requiring isolation or depletion of a supplementary water supply; Appendix 3.1.5 Water Needs Assessment; Appendix 3.1.7 all on aerodrome developments assessed for potential impact on any supplementary water supply; 32.1 plans to allow for short/long term closures ensuring the aerodrome operation is safe to resume following an aircraft accident or incident; 32.2 contingency plans to cope immediately with the loss of all or part of a facility including ATC facilities, passenger terminals, freight facilities, fuel facilities, road access and administration buildings. UNITED ARAB EMIRATES DOCUMENT — worked example of adoption mechanics, NOT a South African requirement and not binding on any reader.',
