    'Adverse weather conditions requiring special action by the airport operator are snow, fog, strong winds, frost, ice and freezing rain (Doc 9137 Part 8 §6.1.1).',
    'It is essential that a communications net be established so that messages from the Meteorological Office giving adequate warning of all the above meteorological phenomena are passed to operations, air traffic control and the airlines (§6.1.2).',
