    'RFFS and associated external response personnel should be made aware of areas that may from time to time become impassable because of weather, and of the location of obstacles both permanent and temporary (§13.3.5.6).',
    'During low visibility procedures it is essential that airport security restricts airside access for vehicles and personnel, prohibited areas are closed off by lighting, contractors working in the manoeuvring area evacuate, and ATC is advised when the checks are complete and safeguarding complete (Doc 9137 Part 8 §6.6.4.2).',
    'Airport operations should arrange for airside patrols to collect blowing objects that cannot be retrieved and are blown onto operational areas, and warn ATC and operations (§6.4.3).',
    'Adverse weather is one of the ten factors in the worst-case location analysis, alongside route, terrain, active runway crossings, aircraft congestion, surface conditions, communications, supplementary water supplies and daylight or darkness (Doc 9137 Part 1 §10.5.7.4).'
