    'ICAO Doc 9137 Part 8 — §6.3 ice, frost and freezing rain; §6.3.1 when ice, frost or freezing rain warnings are received airport operations should respond by ensuring the serviceability of friction test devices and ice warning systems where fitted; §6.3.6 grit and sand as a last resort, use on the runway generally avoided owing to possible adverse effect on turboprop and jet engines at high power; §6.3.6.3 salt not to be used for de-icing or anti-icing on the movement area other than as a mixture of 5 per cent salt, 95 per cent grit for runway edge drains, extreme care to avoid corrosion risk to aircraft',
